# Pronto starting with the Split Inbox on, its default (the fork's phase C, docs/superhuman/
# split.md "UI"): the store reads the Inbox's Important side ahead while the window is built,
# and the window's first view is that one, not a second open; the other side then opens ahead,
# so the first Tab adopts it. Fixture mail; every name and address is fictional.
# Run: tools/headless.sh 62 target/debug/pronto --self-test tests/selftest/split-startup.sealwax-test

desktop tiling
layout-defaults app
fixtures --count 300 --seed 13 --folders single
# Before the window's steps: the sides are on from the start, as in the app.
split-inbox on
list-wait
assert-first-view adopted
assert-split-side important
assert-split-tabs totals
assert-action-state win.split-inbox true
focus list
# After the startup's own work (the reader's engine, the composer's spare editor), as
# perf-split waits: the switches must adopt the side opened ahead; their speed is split-inbox's
# and perf-split's to hold.
sleep 1500
measure-split Tab 2 1000
assert-split-side important
key Tab
assert-split-side other
assert-list-selected 0
